WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.997
Welcome to Module 9. In this module, we are moving from general Python programming into numerical data analysis.

00:00:08.997 --> 00:00:14.892
NumPy is one of the main libraries used for working with numbers efficiently in Python.

00:00:14.892 --> 00:00:23.122
Instead of processing one value at a time, we can organize many values into arrays and perform calculations across the

00:00:23.122 --> 00:00:24.383
entire array.

00:00:24.879 --> 00:00:33.766
We will practice creating arrays, checking their structure, filtering values, reshaping data, calculating summaries,

00:00:33.766 --> 00:00:39.226
generating random values, and performing simple analytical tasks.

00:00:39.226 --> 00:00:44.891
These ideas appear again in Pandas, statistics, machine learning, and many other Python libraries.

00:00:44.891 --> 00:00:49.811
The goal is not to memorize every NumPy function.

00:00:49.811 --> 00:00:59.117
The goal is to become comfortable thinking in arrays and understanding how numerical data is organized and processed.
